    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "CONVERSIONS\n\nPins have types (i64 whole numbers, f64 decimals, bool, String). The compiler converts automatically\nin two safe cases: a whole number into a decimal pin (7 -> 7.0) and ANY value into a String pin\n(7 -> \"7\"). Everything else needs a node: Number To String, Bool To String, Parse Int, String Parse\nFloat (parsing can fail on bad text, so check with Is Number first in real code).",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          210.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "AUTOMATIC\ncount (i64) -> widened (f64) and count -> count_text (String): no conversion node. widened = 123.0, count_text = \"123\".",
        "position": [
          360.0,
          680.0
